== Motivation

Many excellent Petri net model checkers exist, including LoLA @schmidt_lola_2000, TAPAAL @jensen_tapaal_2016,
Charlie @heiner_charlie_2015,
and do not provide access to the underlying theory which made those results possible,
inhibiting the user's ability to learn from the tool.
Those tools that do highlight the theoretical foundations are generally oriented around human-readable explanations,
which are useful for educational purposes but awkward for programmatic use and are not designed to be embedded into
larger software systems.
